-- title:
--   Riemann–Hurwitz inequality for a Kummer extension
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $F$ a field equipped with an $L$-algebra structure which is a function field of one variable over $L$ in the sense that there exists $x \in F$ transcendental over $L$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $L(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $n$ be a natural number whose image in $L$ is nonzero, let $c \in F$, and let $F'$ be a field which is an $F$-algebra and an $L$-algebra compatibly (scalar tower $L \subseteq F \subseteq F'$), which is a splitting field of $X^n - c$ over $F$ and satisfies $[F' : F] = n$. Places of $F/L$ are valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $L$, different from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings; for such a place $P$ and $f \in F$, $\operatorname{ord}_P f$ is the negative of the logarithm of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation of $f$ attached to $P$. For every finite set $S$ of places of $F/L$ the assertion is the inequality $$n \cdot 2\bigl(g(F) - 1\bigr) + \sum_{P \in S}\bigl(n - \gcd(n, |\operatorname{ord}_P c|)\bigr) \le 2\bigl(g(F') - 1\bigr),$$ where $g(F) =$ `genusFF L F` and $g(F') =$ `genusFF L F'` denote the genus computed as the $L$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor, and the greatest common divisor is taken between $n$ and the absolute value of $\operatorname{ord}_P c$. Only this inequality is asserted, with the ramification contribution summed over the chosen finite set $S$ rather than over all places.
--
--   This is the Riemann–Hurwitz genus inequality for the Kummer extension $F' = F(c^{1/n})$ of a function field over an algebraically closed field, in the tame case where $n$ is invertible: the different contributes at least $n - \gcd(n,\operatorname{ord}_P c)$ above each place $P$. It is used to bound the genus of a Kummer base change of a modular function field, in the genus estimate for the Igusa function field of $X_1$ feeding the level-lowering arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_two_mul_genusFF_sub_one_ge_of_isSplittingField_X_pow_sub_C.lean

